{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing","id":416544,"title":"How restoring Pangea can be a good thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-23T09:35:18-08:00","id":416544,"title":"How restoring Pangea can be a good thing?","content":"My Swedish game is about the Bale Hounds, but lately, I try to convince myself to the Pure Tribes, and maybe add them in later. One of major problem with <i>Anshega</i> I have is that their are mostly about propaganda and psychological terror. I know they believe they are all times at war and it need it's sacrifices. But when I would run Pure I would like to make players question <i>their</i> way of doing things as Forsaken. Hinting that maybe their enemies are <b>right</b>, maybe their dogmas are true. And it's Forsaken are doing things wrong.<br /> <br /> One of major points I think I could play this is Pangea. In 1ed corebook, mythical time of Spirit and Flesh being one is - in reality - sounds horrible. Those legions of Spirit-Ridden, Spirit Lords running amok, people crossing randomly the Border Marches - how any of this could be a good thing? How to convince Forsaken that return to this &quot;Eden&quot; would be great for them, humanity and spirits they all try to balance?<br /> <br /> For now I only see an idea &quot;in Pangaea things were different&quot;, but it's too nebulous to make any good argument for Pure elder to young pups or try to win over Forsaken to their cause. Any help in here you can see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:39:13-08:00","id":416561,"title":"","content":"Part of the Pure belief system involves the idea that they were much more powerful before the death of Father Wolf. With the bringing back of Pangaea or Father Wolf, they will regain this strength that will put them back on top, power-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:56:11-08:00","id":416578,"title":"","content":"Wyrdhamster's terminology is wrong; it's &quot;Pangaea&quot;. <br /> <br /> Why wouldn't you want to join them? It's the winner's side. They get to have strength in numbers. They get to have the most powerful spirit allies (what must it be like, you wonder - not to be afraid of spirits anymore? Not to be scared for your life every single time you enter the Shadow? Not to have the threat of being jumped by freak shadow beings and Ridden hanging over you all the time?). And then there's the freedom granted to them by their dogma that the Forsaken can never have - running wild and free, hunting and killing as you like, never looking back at the consequences. <br /> <br /> It's important to remember, however, that the Pure's idea of what Pangaea was like is wrong; even in the context of their own constructed propaganda/mythology. <br /> <br /> What's Pangaea? And what Pangaea, precisely, is it that the Pure want? Is it Pangaea as the hunter's paradise, in which humanity is one animal among many, in which predator and prey exist in perfect balance, and the few offenders can easily be defeated by an appropriate punisher figure like Father Wolf or the Uratha?<br /> <br /> Or is it Pangaea as the flawed paradise that it was in its last days, a hell threatening to consume the world, in which humanity was defenseless to a host of beings as destructive as the Spinner Hag, the Plague King or the Zmei?<br /> <br /> There's Pangaea, an age/realm/place that once was, and there's whatever it is the Pure are trying to create. One of these things might not be the same as the other. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:40:57-08:00","id":416638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416578#post416578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrdhamster's terminology is wrong; it's &quot;Pangaea&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for that, in Polish term is spelled without second &quot;a&quot;. But in English it's longer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416578#post416578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't you want to join them? It's the winner's side. They get to have strength in numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They win only in recent 20 years. And the <b>Pure</b> book mentiones the history of Uratha is Pandalum of winning by Forsaken and Pure Tribes in exchange, for millenia. Not too mention that winning - for now - the war by one side does not makes it arguments a realistic or convincing. It's just point they have tactical advantage.<br /> <br /> In other word, thing that Pure are winning now, does not make them right on the rising of Pangaea ( and any other thing ). / At least it that what new pups and possible converts of Pure could answer / <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416578#post416578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get to have the most powerful spirit allies (what must it be like, you wonder - not to be afraid of spirits anymore? Not to be scared for your life every single time you enter the Shadow? Not to have the threat of being jumped by freak shadow beings and Ridden hanging over you all the time?). And then there's the freedom granted to them by their dogma that the Forsaken can never have - running wild and free, hunting and killing as you like, never looking back at the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one thing, sure. But still, being spirits favored is somehow antitheme to Forsaken ideology, and by this - it's not suited as argument to convert to the Pure Tribes. It would be like saying &quot;we know, you conservatices, do not like gays - so we have all the gays in here to party with you. Come to us.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's important to remember, however, that the Pure's idea of what Pangaea was like is wrong; even in the context of their own constructed propaganda/mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416578#post416578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's Pangaea? And what Pangaea, precisely, is it that the Pure want? Is it Pangaea as the hunter's paradise, in which humanity is one animal among many, in which predator and prey exist in perfect balance, and the few offenders can easily be defeated by an appropriate punisher figure like Father Wolf or the Uratha?<br /> <br /> Or is it Pangaea as the flawed paradise that it was in its last days, a hell threatening to consume the world, in which humanity was defenseless to a host of beings as destructive as the Spinner Hag, the Plague King or the Zmei?<br /> <br /> There's Pangaea, an age/realm/place that once was, and there's whatever it is the Pure are trying to create. One of these things might not be the same as the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is excelent question - WHAT is Pangaea in general Pure population? How is this better than now leaving world?<br /> <br /> Because beliving &quot;it will be better, it will be Paradise&quot; with seeing how spirits work is wishfull thinking, not rational goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:58:24-08:00","id":416651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416638#post416638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one thing, sure. But still, being spirits favored is somehow antitheme to Forsaken ideology, and by this - it's not suited as argument to convert to the Pure Tribes. It would be like saying &quot;we know, you conservatices, do not like gays - so we have all the gays in here to party with you. Come to us.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't understand; which is hardly surprising.<br /> <br /> As a Forsaken, a whole lot of shadowy beings what you dead. As a Pure, quite a few of those shadowy beings are on your side.<br /> <br /> A higher chance of survival is a very strong motivation for pretty much every sane person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:03:31-08:00","id":416655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416638#post416638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember, however, that the Pure's idea of what Pangaea was like is wrong; even in the context of their own constructed propaganda/mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get that from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:35:00-08:00","id":416701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416651#post416651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't understand; which is hardly surprising.<br /> <br /> As a Forsaken, a whole lot of shadowy beings what you dead. As a Pure, quite a few of those shadowy beings are on your side.<br /> <br /> A higher chance of survival is a very strong motivation for pretty much every sane person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that can be reasoned with, but it's still more &quot;we have backup, join us&quot; than &quot;we have right - and can prove it - join us&quot;, what was a point of this topic. Idea was to convince Forsaken that Pure <i>ideology</i> has sense, not their tactical advantages ( that can diminish with Pendulum of History swinging with Forsaken win),<br /> <br /> Like Seers of Throne convincing Pentacle mages they do right things to be done - and not on their &quot;we have Martiny and every luxury&quot;, but on dogmatic, &quot;you must work for Exarchs or the world will be destroyed&quot; kinda thing. In that light - HOW restoring the Pangaea is a good thing? On purely pragmatic level, not &quot;we will be at the top, even if now we are not&quot; wishful thinking?<br /> <br /> I still see only &quot;we will win this war&quot; on Pure side, not &quot;we have right with our point of view&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416655#post416655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you get that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least if not Spirits become suddenly ruthless egocentric beasts in time of Fall of Pangaea, the Predators Paradise would be filled with half-fleshed horrors and Spirit Lords ruling the humans, at least till Urfarah shows up. How this kind - based on now seen Shadow - version of Pangaea could be a good thing? How this could convince the Forsaken Uratha that spend a decades harmonizing Flesh and Spirit - that Pure could be right and Pangaea should be raised again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:55:54-08:00","id":416715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416701#post416701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least if not Spirits become suddenly ruthless egocentric beasts in time of Fall of Pangaea, the Predators Paradise would be filled with half-fleshed horrors and Spirit Lords ruling the humans, at least till Urfarah shows up. How this kind - based on now seen Shadow - version of Pangaea could be a good thing? How this could convince the Forsaken Uratha that spend a decades harmonizing Flesh and Spirit - that Pure could be right and Pangaea should be raised again?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Forsaken, not just Pure, legends about Pangaea, the place existed with humans and spirits living together already. While it doesn't seem likely it was the most peaceful of existences, the legends state that Pangaea depended less on the material world. It seems like it was more of its own world.<br /> <br /> Spirits hate werewolves because they took the Predator's paradise away and then decided they were still going to police them. It's one thing to keep predatory spirits in the Predator's Paradise, it's an entirely other thing to keep them imprisoned in a fading reflection of the material world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:14:25-08:00","id":416739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416715#post416715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Forsaken, not just Pure, legends about Pangaea, the place existed with humans and spirits living together already. While it doesn't seem likely it was the most peaceful of existences, the legends state that Pangaea depended less on the material world. It seems like it was more of its own world.<br /> <br /> Spirits hate werewolves because they took the Predator's paradise away and then decided they were still going to police them. It's one thing to keep predatory spirits in the Predator's Paradise, it's an entirely other thing to keep them imprisoned in a fading reflection of the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's work with that. Assuming that Predator's Paradise was a more less restricted on the idea of &quot;spirits wrong, humans good&quot;, what could it look like? Like Japan in <b>Princess Mononoke</b>, with great spirits walking beside humans next to their arms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/4OiMOHRDs14\" data-code=\"4OiMOHRDs14\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4OiMOHRDs14/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:33:00-08:00","id":416760,"title":"","content":"There was war in Princess Mononoke too, it's not all peace and love. But from what we've seen, sure. A fantasy world, for sure.<br /> <br /> It's not about spirits wrong, human's good. Humans suffered from the fall as well, that's one of the reasons they're affected so much by Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:45:47-08:00","id":416767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416760#post416760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was war in Princess Mononoke too, it's not all peace and love. But from what we've seen, sure. A fantasy world, for sure.<br /> <br /> It's not about spirits wrong, human's good. Humans suffered from the fall as well, that's one of the reasons they're affected so much by Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Princess Mononoke is a great example of how both sides of this equation kind of suck. There's not a good guy or a bad guy on either side, there's people(and People) doing what they need to take care of people they've decided to help, and that just happens pit 'civilization' against 'the wilderness'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:47:38-08:00","id":416769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416760#post416760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about spirits wrong, human's good. Humans suffered from the fall as well, that's one of the reasons they're affected so much by Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits become egomaniacal conspirators, humans get werewolf-related amnesia (Lunacy) - how this is not &quot;spirits bad, humans good&quot;?<br /> <br /> And to return a topic in to more of the line - how could Fall of Pangaea made Luna &quot;Mother Bitch&quot;, as some Pure call her? What could be wrong with her, beside that she is distant to her children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:53:58-08:00","id":416775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416769#post416769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to return a topic in to more of the line - how could Fall of Pangaea made Luna &quot;Mother Bitch&quot;, as some Pure call her? What could be wrong with her, beside that she is distant to her children?</div> </div> </div> </div>Father Wolf was weakened by the creation of his children with Luna. Some Pure believe that was her plan all along. Plus she cursed them all, then gave a mild reprieve to those who swear to serve her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:54:25-08:00","id":416776,"title":"","content":"Because the humans are protecting and providing a life for the neglected and spurned members of society and the spirits are irrational beings who agitate the situation way beyond what they should?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:44:38-08:00","id":416859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How to convince Forsaken that return to this &quot;Eden&quot; would be great for them, humanity and spirits they all try to balance? </div> </div> </div>Do the Pure care about Humanity all that much? My impression of them was more that they see it as effectively a resource. I imagine that's what'd be attractive about them; they articulate a vision where werewolves are free of their thankless duties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:55:17-08:00","id":416864,"title":"","content":"Legends say it's the Fall that caused their reproductive problems. Undoing that would really get rid of their need for humanity at all. Or just moving to second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:36:57-08:00","id":417082,"title":"","content":"The original lore also suggested that the unihar are representative of how the forsaken were in the before time. They're irrelevant now, same with 1e harmony. You find much fewer harmony broken pure these days, as it's more about balance and less on atrocities. Sure there's a beastly low harmony predator king or a really high harmony iron master, but for the most part I imagine balance (or some semblance of) is easier. Even for the bale hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T21:34:48-08:00","id":417167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=416859#post416859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Pure care about Humanity all that much? My impression of them was more that they see it as effectively a resource. I imagine that's what'd be attractive about them; they articulate a vision where werewolves are free of their thankless duties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think about tired Forsaken that want to leave his duties and joins Pure, yes. But most of Forsakens still care about humans and how Pure treat them ( like cattle, in reality ) is too much to them to bear. I could see individual converts, but not the mass changes in the Tribes association ( from Forsaken to Pure ) that books talk about. Pure seems still, in their ideology, to much antagonistic for most Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Also, loosing of Auspices is very large sacrifice on the character side - are not any mechanics to fill for it in <b>Pure</b> book?<br /> <br /> Urgh. whenever I try to make Pure more convinving for Forsaken players, I get on next wall of &quot;they are so 'animals in human skins'&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, good point about Unihir - it would have sense in 1ed that Pangaea could solve this and Harmony problem. But now they just gone *puff* Maybe it's a sign that Pangaea is coming? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Less restrictive Harmony and no problem with werewolves spirit children? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-24-2015, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:23:10-08:00","id":417337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can think about dried Forsaken that want to leave his duites and joines Pure, yes. But most of Forsakens still care about humans and how Pure treat them ( like cattle, in reality ) is too much to them to bear. </div> </div> </div>But they are cattle (to a degree). I mean, the Uratha seem to naturally view humans as prey (wanting to eat people is pretty dehumanising). That's before you get to the issues with death rage and such, which require that the Uratha be vigilant around humans at all times. There's plenty of reason to think that a lot of Forsaken would have a degree of resentment towards humanity in general.<br /> <br /> Plus, I don't think the Pure actually tell you you can't be nice to your particular group of humans if you want. That's the kind of thinking I'd see appealling to the pack mentality. I'd guess most uratha care about some humans (their families and close associates), not humanity in totality.<br /> <br /> Thing is, this is all in-character motivation. It's tricky to convey that to players who don't actually feel any of these pressures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:32:39-08:00","id":417519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417337#post417337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus, I don't think the Pure actually tell you you can't be nice to your particular group of humans if you want. That's the kind of thinking I'd see appealling to the pack mentality. I'd guess most uratha care about some humans (their families and close associates), not humanity in totality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Predator Kings, who will in fact need to at least dislike humanity in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:51:02-08:00","id":417581,"title":"","content":"as a predator king disliking humanity is second nature, id imagine. It takes a particular kind of romantic to join that tribe. Never mind their god is hate incarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:36:10-08:00","id":417608,"title":"","content":"The Predator King ideology is attractive to the wrong kind of people because it justifies the worst kind of excesses, it tells young werewolves that being a monster and killing anyone they like is their natural right, and it gives them someone to blame for everything that goes and went wrong with their lives. There's lots and lots and lots of people in the real world who are really into that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> The great thing about the Pure is also the great thing about the Seers of the Throne - their ideologies are very accessible in the context of ordinary people and the way they work. If you think there's nothing in you and your personality that supports a way of thinking that dehumanizes other people the way the Pure and the Seers of the Throne are prone to do, you are very likely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:41:58-08:00","id":417612,"title":"","content":"Predator Kings certainly appeal to the teenage misanthrope that I was and still occasionally flirt with being when I see really nasty things that people do to each other.<br /> <br /> Then again that's the same immature part of me that Bale Hounds appeal to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:14:26-08:00","id":417628,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds are often maligned as pure evil, way out there freaks by people who misunderstand them or haven't read the books; but, if anything, it's far easier to join the Bale Hounds or to understand the Bale Hound way of thinking in out of character terms in comparison to the Pure. <br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are people. A Bale Hound is every person, on a bad day. <br /> <br /> You don't join the Bale Hounds by approaching the gods of sin and asking to join up, you join them by being yourself - on a bad day. <br /> <br /> Your grandfather dies. There's grief and there's shock, but there's also rage, rage at the doctors who botched the surgery that should have been a very easy operation, who didn't take the necessary precautions. <br /> <br /> The new girl gets the promotion that you have been promised. It's probably simply because she's more attractive than you. <br /> <br /> Your wife has stopped sleeping with you. She simply doesn't find you interesting any more. She's probably sleeping around. <br /> <br /> Doesn't that make you angry? Doesn't that make you feel wronged? Shouldn't <i>someone </i>pay? <br /> <br /> Add to this the emotional, deeply passionate nature of the Forsaken race. We all have felt really, really angry at one point or another in our lives. When werewolves feel angry, they don't feel like shouting or hitting someone the way we do, they feel like transforming into 3 meters of raging wolf-death, tearing someone's throat out and drowning him in his own blood - and they sometimes cannot help doing exactly that. <br /> <br /> The Bale Hound philosophy isn't scary because it's about alienation from humanity or worship of Outer Evil, it's scary because it's about human vices, human emotions and human feelings gone wrong. What makes the Bale Hounds tragic figures is that their horror is human horror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:15:34-08:00","id":417630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417608#post417608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Predator King ideology is attractive to the wrong kind of people because it justifies the worst kind of excesses, it tells young werewolves that being a monster and killing anyone they like is their natural right, and it gives them someone to blame for everything that goes and went wrong with their lives. There's lots and lots and lots of people in the real world who are really into that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> The great thing about the Pure is also the great thing about the Seers of the Throne - their ideologies are very accessible in the context of ordinary people and the way they work. If you think there's nothing in you and your personality that supports a way of thinking that dehumanizes other people the way the Pure and the Seers of the Throne are prone to do, you are very likely wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I think trying to find why the restoring of Pangaea is a &quot;Good Thing&quot; is... The wrong thing to be focusing on. <br /> <br /> The appeal of joining the Pure is not in their mythology. It's in the benefits the Pure provide werewolves with. Safety in numbers and more powerful spirits to watch over them. Encouraged to revel in freedom of their baser nature. <br /> <br /> The Pure are meant to be cults, which are focused on manipulating its members for real and tangible benefits for the leaders based on the veneer of a mythology/spirituality that falls apart on close introspection. <br /> <br /> Restoring Pangaea is supposed to bring about a utopia for werewolf-kind because of fabled nostalgia of how everything was better before those assholes ruined everything and because this powerful spirit tells me so and because shut up I'm busy and you're asking too many questions, now go enjoy your hookers and blow because tomorrow night I need you to fight for me. <br /> <br /> Even if you realize that &quot;restoring Pangaea&quot; is pointless drivel, it doesn't subtract from the real benefits of having safety in numbers, the protection by a big ass spirit or the excuse to exercise your bigotry as much as you want. <br /> <br /> I'm largely okay with this because it comes across as very human to do, in a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:18:07-08:00","id":417639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417630#post417630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I think trying to find why the restoring of Pangaea is a &quot;Good Thing&quot; is... The wrong thing to be focusing on.</div> </div> </div> </div>People including me tried to tell wyrdhamster exactly that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417630#post417630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm largely okay with this because it comes across as very human to do, in a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely the point, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:51:04-08:00","id":417807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417630#post417630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The appeal of joining the Pure is not in their mythology. It's in the benefits the Pure provide werewolves with. Safety in numbers and more powerful spirits to watch over them. Encouraged to revel in freedom of their baser nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those benefits come to Forsaken only when they start to agree with ideology, And even then, converts from Forsaken to Pure are treated badly, at most as Omega in Pure packs. Why then join your enemy that is not have compelling ideology, have clashing mythology with what you fight for and all benefits are last to you as you will be treated badly in their group?<br /> <br /> In other way - I want my eventual Forsaken players to consider Pure offers. Not to become next slaves to them, but in the way &quot;those Pure could have right, Forsaken could be wrong&quot;. Because when you portray them as them sound in first chapter of <b>Pure</b> book, they can convert Forsaken only on basis &quot;join us or die&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yes, I look for compelling parts in Pure ideology and mythology to tempt possible Forsaken players with that. Benefits coming last on this list, as players do not look on them in &quot;dark, tragic, heroic game&quot; that the <b>Werewolf</b> is. When you play Forsaken, it's because you believe that Flesh and Spirit relations should be better, that werewolves should goes in the footsteps of Father Wolf in Pangaea times, and show &quot;human&quot; side to the Pure.<br /> <br /> Try to convince this kind ideological characters to Pure Tribes, not with &quot;you are surrounded, we are more numerous&quot; - as those tactical advantages are based on time and local demographics, not the ideology of Pure.<br /> <br /> What in Pure dogmas could compel Forsaken to join them? <b>Micheal</b> pointed freedom from duty the Forsaken are sustaining. Clearly we have also Pangaea as specific Paradise all Uratha are compelled with. Other things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-24-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:18:58-08:00","id":417862,"title":"","content":"The Fire-Touched, who receive the most converts, have a belief in a Hunter's Paradise called <i>Taga Dan</i> that all Pure may choose to go to when they die in good faith. The Forsaken, they say, become mad Lunes upon their deaths as their Auspice renown bands become shackles that enslave them to the moon. Only becoming Pure will save them from this awful fate and open up the path to <i>Taga Dan. </i>The Fire-Touched tell and abide no lies, and so this story is true: Purity is salvation from the damnation and deception of the Moon.<br /> <br /> When you see how the Shadow is so easily Wounded by the filth and malice of the humans it can be easy to hate them. Their works bring ruin, their actions cause pain, and their ways of life breed weakness in what presumes to be the dominant species on this earth. The Predator Kings have an answer to this pathetic state of affairs: &quot;Honor nothing of human craft.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws have little to appeal to converts, and they like it this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-24-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:19:09-08:00","id":417864,"title":"","content":"An alternative tactic would be to look at the way the Forsaken fail to achieve their ambitions of fulfilling the duty of Father Wolf. I mean, if your local Forsaken community are mired in hypocrisy... well, at least the Pure are honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:11:07-08:00","id":417950,"title":"","content":"I honestly find the Forsaken buy-in the hardest to believe.<br /> <br /> Someone goes through their First Change, is probably terrified or on the run after doing something horrible. Then some other werewolf finds them, 'Don't worry, you're just suffering because we killed Father Wolf over three thousand years ago. Just swear this Oath to the Moon, and you can go start this job. There's no pay, no health plan beyond those natural abilities of yours, and no time off, and you can only retire the hard way, when someone or something kills you. But hey, look on the bright side, you can travel to another world. Hm? No, no women there, just monsters. And most of them hate you.'<br /> <br /> I mean I appreciate it's more of a duty than a job, but joining up is taking responsibility for a 'crime' committed thousands of years ago that may have only occurred in myth, the danger of being a target for the spirit world and other various enemies, the sexual and other restrictions of the Oath of the Moon and the lack of time off it's like signing up to join the military, police academy and one of the more strict religions all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:14:36-08:00","id":417957,"title":"","content":"The sexual restrictions are off the table now in 2e, but otherwise you're on the ball.<br /> <br /> Of course I suspect most Forsaken are as much believers in what their Tribes tell them now days as many people who belong to any given religion are: Sorta.<br /> <br /> The Tribes of the Moon still come with benefits in the form of giving access to Gifts and other such concretely useful things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:35:12-08:00","id":417979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417957#post417957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sexual restrictions are off the table now in 2e, but otherwise you're on the ball.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know unihar don't exist anymore, and Uratha can reproduce, but is that part of the Oath of the Moon being taken out as well or are we still cleaving to the herd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:40:36-08:00","id":417999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417979#post417979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know unihar don't exist anymore, and Uratha can reproduce, but is that part of the Oath of the Moon being taken out as well or are we still cleaving to the herd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cleaving to the Herd is still there, but it does not explicitly refer to reproduction. It is more a call to remain connected to the human herd, which can be done more readily now that including humans in werewolf packs is the norm. Some fringe territories have packs who take this to mean werewolves shouldn't breed with one another, but that seems to be a minority position now.<br /> <br /> This is what I remember from the writer comments on the Open Development blog, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:00:18-08:00","id":418152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417950#post417950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly find the Forsaken buy-in the hardest to believe.<br /> <br /> Someone goes through their First Change, is probably terrified or on the run after doing something horrible. Then some other werewolf finds them, 'Don't worry, you're just suffering because we killed Father Wolf over three thousand years ago. Just swear this Oath to the Moon, and you can go start this job. There's no pay, no health plan beyond those natural abilities of yours, and no time off, and you can only retire the hard way, when someone or something kills you. But hey, look on the bright side, you can travel to another world. Hm? No, no women there, just monsters. And most of them hate you.'<br /> <br /> I mean I appreciate it's more of a duty than a job, but joining up is taking responsibility for a 'crime' committed thousands of years ago that may have only occurred in myth, the danger of being a target for the spirit world and other various enemies, the sexual and other restrictions of the Oath of the Moon and the lack of time off it's like signing up to join the military, police academy and one of the more strict religions all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you don't need to join the Forsaken by swearing the Oath. Ghost Wolves are Forsaken - right after the Change the spirit brand identifying your auspice is lit in your half-flesh- and that's the most Forsaken they'll ever be. No spiritual allies, no totem, no pack.<br /> <br /> The thing with the Forsaken is that it's always your choice. It's your choice which Wolf Deity you swear to emulate. It's your choice which pack you join.<br /> <br /> It's your choice if you wanna join a tribe to begin with.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that if the Pure found you first. Ripping those silver brands is a bitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-24-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:26:21-08:00","id":418239,"title":"","content":"Have you read their initiation rites? The brands may well be the easiest part in some cases. You just have to sit there and let your mind go kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:15:43-08:00","id":418282,"title":"","content":"I always forget about the Ghost Wolves. In a way that's even worse. I'm surprised there's not more blasphemies and other options available aside from Pure and Bale Hounds. I liked Acrozatarim's werewolf cults. There's probably other things out there to serve and ways to get rid of the brands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:24:13-08:00","id":418285,"title":"","content":"The Blasphemies book is all over that. Still, I agree; I am all over the twisted wolf-cults.<br /> <br /> Shadows of the UK is full of Ghost Wolf packs; Ghost Wolves and Bale Hounds are ridiculously prevalent on the British Isles compared to most of the world. And if we take Acrozatarim's Paris as an example Ghost Wolves are just as prevalent there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:43:13-08:00","id":418305,"title":"","content":"I take most things writers do as canon. &gt;.&gt; even if it isn't. &quot;What? He wrote the core? Cool I know how Paris is now!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T00:02:48-08:00","id":418455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417807#post417807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those benefits come to Forsaken only when they start to agree with ideology, And even then, converts from Forsaken to Pure are treated badly, at most as Omega in Pure packs. Why then join your enemy that is not have compelling ideology, have clashing mythology with what you fight for and all benefits are last to you as you will be treated badly in their group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because even if you're treated as the lowest of the low of the Pure Pack you joined, treated as the &quot;Omega&quot;, <i>you're still a member of the Pack</i>. And because of that, you're still entitled to the protection of the Pack. The Pack's alpha is still responsible for your actions, your safety is still their concern and the concern of the Pack's Totem. Even if that concern is only so much <i>that no one outside of the Pack can treat you like shit</i>. Because if someone from outside the Pack disses you? They've insulted your Pack's Alpha and now need to deal with <i><b>THEM</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Forget ideology. The compelling argument here is, if aimed at a Ghost Wolf, &quot;You are alone. You have no one to watch out for you. Spirits hate you and other werewolves treat you with paranoia. Cast that aside, renounce Luna and join us. I and our god will protect you. If someone outside of us wants to hurt or kill you, they have to fight through all of us, because you would be of our Pack and you would be mine and our god's and we protect what is ours.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, you'd be the lowest member of the Pack. But that just means you only have a lot to prove, right? It's your responsibility to show that you're not the weakest of the Pack and if you can show your strength, if you can show how much of a help you can be to your Pack and your Alpha, that means they'd respect you, right?<br /> <br /> ...And that's the thinking that traps people. The feeling that their situation is their fault, that things would be better if they only DID things better.<br /> <br /> This is why when you think of Pure converting people? The Pure aren't really targeting Forsaken, or at least not Forsaken who are set in their ways. They're targeting the fresh blood. Ghost Wolves who don't have allegiances set. Young Uratha who don't know whats going on and crave simple answers for why they feel the urges they have. Forsaken who have just started to walk their moonlit path and still have questions and fears about a world they're desperately trying to understand.<br /> <br /> And that's how the Pure convert. By playing on FEAR. Fear of themselves (&quot;We can teach you what you are.&quot;), fear of the unknown (&quot;We can tell you why the world is as it is.&quot;, it doesn't have to be TRUE, just answers, even if lies), fear of outsiders (&quot;Obey and we will protect you.&quot;)<br /> <br /> The Pure could be preaching worship of the Great Moon Cheese Spirit, usurped by the Luna Witch Spirit, and that wouldn't change the fundamental benefits that the Pure provide their members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T00:06:45-08:00","id":418458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417862#post417862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fire-Touched, who receive the most converts, have a belief in a Hunter's Paradise called <i>Taga Dan</i> that all Pure may choose to go to when they die in good faith. The Forsaken, they say, become mad Lunes upon their deaths as their Auspice renown bands become shackles that enslave them to the moon. Only becoming Pure will save them from this awful fate and open up the path to <i>Taga Dan. </i>The Fire-Touched tell and abide no lies, and so this story is true: Purity is salvation from the damnation and deception of the Moon.<br /> <br /> When you see how the Shadow is so easily Wounded by the filth and malice of the humans it can be easy to hate them. Their works bring ruin, their actions cause pain, and their ways of life breed weakness in what presumes to be the dominant species on this earth. The Predator Kings have an answer to this pathetic state of affairs: &quot;Honor nothing of human craft.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws have little to appeal to converts, and they like it this way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Fire-Touched angle is actually a really good one to bring up! Considering humanity's history with religion, this fits very well with previous religions that Uratha might have been members of before their First Change, where having the silver branding afterwards can too easily be seen as being <i>afflicted </i>by them, rather than awarded them, by Luna's hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:40:41-08:00","id":418516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=418239#post418239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read their initiation rites? The brands may well be the easiest part in some cases. You just have to sit there and let your mind go kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I was done with the Pure source book before you even knew what a Pure was, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:32:04-08:00","id":418707,"title":"","content":"&gt;.&gt; considering I bought the books back when they came out I doubt that. But hey let's keep being unecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:32:21-08:00","id":418708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=417807#post417807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other way - I want my eventual Forsaken players to consider Pure offers. Not to become next slaves to them, but in the way &quot;those Pure could have right, Forsaken could be wrong&quot;. Because when you portray them as them sound in first chapter of <b>Pure</b> book, they can convert Forsaken only on basis &quot;join us or die&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yes, I look for compelling parts in Pure ideology and mythology to tempt possible Forsaken players with that. Benefits coming last on this list, as players do not look on them in &quot;dark, tragic, heroic game&quot; that the <b>Werewolf</b> is. When you play Forsaken, it's because you believe that Flesh and Spirit relations should be better, that werewolves should goes in the footsteps of Father Wolf in Pangaea times, and show &quot;human&quot; side to the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played around with this a good deal in my chronicle - although I'll say first up that I make a few changes and assumptions that other Storytellers might not go for; I downplay horror, and make the Pure less rabidly threatening, trying instead to present them as sympathetic antagonists with a competing ideology.<br /> I also play around with myth and blasphemy, which is why I think you might be interested in my approach.<br /> <br /> The Pure, as I present them (in this chronicle, at least), want all those same things you said Forsaken want: better relations between Flesh and Spirit, to follow Father Wolf's example. They claim, though, that the Forsaken's desires are being manipulated by an envious, irrational alien tyrant; whereas the Pure approach will heal the world. And they try to only let outsiders see evidence which supports they're right.<br /> <br /> They key ideology I've given to the local Pure (especially Fire-Touched), is that everything wrong in the Shadow is caused by Luna - but proper things do exist, and they serve those. Luna's title of &quot;Queen of the Shadow&quot; might have some literal truth to it in my game: there's been implications (in my setting; not published) that she controls how and when material resonance crosses the Gauntlet to become Essence. The Pure claim this drives otherwise decent spirits to abuse the material out of hunger, while any who submit to Luna get tainted by her madness, and turn cruel, alien, and warped in their purpose.<br /> <br /> In contrast, my Fire-Touched serve the incarnae natural to earth: emotions, nature and element spirits, ancient conceptuals. These are spirits born of Earth; these are the spirits meant to rule it - the influence of celestials can only corrupt what exists here. They claim some spirits are &quot;honest&quot;, that they know their place in the world's ecosystem, and can be reasoned with, befriended, and beneficial to both realms (and that Gurim Ur reveals such spirits to them); if these spirits are given power, and allowed to play in the material, they'll improve things - is one of the philosophies. As a result, they're well liked (and feared) throughout the Shadow.<br /> <br /> One scene I used to emphasize this was I had the players led through a Pure territory by a Predator King shaman. Bunches of spirits were hanging out in Twilight. As they passed a clump of flowers, a gaffling meekly approached and offered chimiage of its own essence to the Predator King, who then casually used &quot;plant growth&quot; on the flowers to return to the gift. --An utter reversal of how things are for the Forsaken. This is the Pangaea they try to restore.<br /> <br /> <br /> [I should note: my PCs now have better relations with the Pure than with the local Forsaken - brokering peace with them has been the longest-running goal of this chronicle. One of the players actually converted to the Fire-Touched, although he did so for the more personal, human reason of regaining the last living connection to his former pack (a dead packmate's nephew, which he got to meet and help out, is Fire-Touched) and only on the caveat that he could remain part of the players' pack (sparing him from the terrible things that happen behind closed doors).]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:44:37-08:00","id":418719,"title":"","content":"That's probably how I would do it seraph. If everything is constant horror you wind up desensitizing your players. &quot;Oh another rapist cannibal monster? Oh boy...&quot; The humanizing approach brings them out with more flare then the traditional antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:19:26-08:00","id":418905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416544-how-restoring-pangea-can-be-a-good-thing?p=418708#post418708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played around with this a good deal in my chronicle - although I'll say first up that I make a few changes and assumptions that other Storytellers might not go for; I downplay horror, and make the Pure less rabidly threatening, trying instead to present them as sympathetic antagonists with a competing ideology.I also play around with myth and blasphemy, which is why I think you might be interested in my approach.<br /> <br /> The Pure, as I present them (in this chronicle, at least), want all those same things you said Forsaken want: better relations between Flesh and Spirit, to follow Father Wolf's example. They claim, though, that the Forsaken's desires are being manipulated by an envious, irrational alien tyrant; whereas the Pure approach will heal the world. And they try to only let outsiders see evidence which supports they're right.<br /> <br /> They key ideology I've given to the local Pure (especially Fire-Touched), is that everything wrong in the Shadow is caused by Luna - but proper things do exist, and they serve those. Luna's title of &quot;Queen of the Shadow&quot; might have some literal truth to it in my game: there's been implications (in my setting; not published) that she controls how and when material resonance crosses the Gauntlet to become Essence. The Pure claim this drives otherwise decent spirits to abuse the material out of hunger, while any who submit to Luna get tainted by her madness, and turn cruel, alien, and warped in their purpose.<br /> <br /> In contrast, my Fire-Touched serve the incarnae natural to earth: emotions, nature and element spirits, ancient conceptuals. These are spirits born of Earth; these are the spirits meant to rule it - the influence of celestials can only corrupt what exists here. They claim some spirits are &quot;honest&quot;, that they know their place in the world's ecosystem, and can be reasoned with, befriended, and beneficial to both realms (and that Gurim Ur reveals such spirits to them); if these spirits are given power, and allowed to play in the material, they'll improve things - is one of the philosophies. As a result, they're well liked (and feared) throughout the Shadow.<br /> <br /> One scene I used to emphasize this was I had the players led through a Pure territory by a Predator King shaman. Bunches of spirits were hanging out in Twilight. As they passed a clump of flowers, a gaffling meekly approached and offered chimiage of its own essence to the Predator King, who then casually used &quot;plant growth&quot; on the flowers to return to the gift. --An utter reversal of how things are for the Forsaken. This is the Pangaea they try to restore.<br /> <br /> <br /> [I should note: my PCs now have better relations with the Pure than with the local Forsaken - brokering peace with them has been the longest-running goal of this chronicle. One of the players actually converted to the Fire-Touched, although he did so for the more personal, human reason of regaining the last living connection to his former pack (a dead packmate's nephew, which he got to meet and help out, is Fire-Touched) and only on the caveat that he could remain part of the players' pack (sparing him from the terrible things that happen behind closed doors).]</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure ( pun intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) awesomness! It's exactly what I was looking - and gone to the same conclusion on today reading of Fire-Touched and connecting Titles of Luna from <b>Lore of the Forsaken</b><i>. </i>In reality, really, the Moon can be subduing werewolves race and is the one responsible in killing the Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}